    "intro": [
      {
        "title": "The two verbs everything starts with",
        "title_cz": "Dvě slovesa, kterými všechno začíná",
        "body": "Almost every first sentence in English uses one of two verbs: **be** (am / is / are) and **have**.\n**be** says who or what somebody is. **have** says what somebody has.\nCzech can leave out the person — *Jsem student.* English cannot: you must say **I am a student.**",
        "note_cz": "Podmět (I, you, he…) se v angličtině nikdy nevynechává."
      },
      {
        "title": "You will use these frames",
        "frames": [
          "I am a …",
          "You are my …",
          "This is my …",
          "He is a …",
          "My name is …",
          "I have a …",
          "Do you have a …?"
        ],
        "note": "Before a job you need **a** or **an**: *He is a doctor*, never *He is doctor*.",
        "note_cz": "U povolání se v angličtině používá a / an."
      }
    ],
